---
description: How to use the Sentivel MCP tools when the user asks about monitoring, uptime, status pages, incidents or on-call
alwaysApply: false
---

- Call `sentivel_whoami` first. It returns the workspace and the role, and the role decides which tools will work.
- If the user belongs to more than one workspace, call `sentivel_list_workspaces` and ask which one before you create anything.
- List before you create. Check `sentivel_list_monitors`, `sentivel_list_components` and `sentivel_list_status_pages` so you don't add duplicates.
- Ask before you delete anything or post an incident update. Incident updates show on a public status page.
- Write incident updates for the customers who read the status page: what is affected, what you know, and when the next update comes. Leave out internal names, hostnames and stack traces.
- Member invites, role changes and billing are not available to tools. Send the user to the Sentivel dashboard for those.
